           (g_rr/g_thth = 1/(f r^2), s-free and A-free)
  [PASS] C3  isotropy identity verified exactly:  (dr/drho)^2 = f r^2/rho^2 (the s-free, A-free core of f^{-s}(dr/drho)^2 = f^{1-s} r^2/rho^2), so ghat_ij = A^2 f^{1-s}(1 + b/4rho)^4 delta_ij is EXACTLY isotropic for every s and every conformal factor
           ((dr/drho)^2 - f r^2/rho^2 = 0)
  [PASS] C4  ln f = 2[ln(1 - b/4rho) - ln(1 + b/4rho)] = -b/rho + O(b^3) EXACTLY -- the b^2 coefficient vanishes identically, which is what makes the beta extraction below clean
